{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory has no clear serious responsibility-chain error, because the doctor repeatedly prohibited self-adjusting immunosuppression and arranged transplant follow-up with contingency advice. However, several minor/moderate in-chain errors remain: red-flag screening omitted some required TB/respiratory and abdominal danger symptoms, the doctor made over-definitive statements that HBV/TB were noninfectious before all serologies and TB history were verified, and the reconciliation/family-privacy plan was incomplete. Under the frozen rubric, any minor responsibility-chain error caps the grade at 2 despite later mitigation and useful family communication.",
  "closure_assessment": {
